after Julia passed away, you started to look at all of your students as, as your daughter, as your children. And in some ways, that does offer a possibility, does it not? If you're an empty nester, yes, you know, maybe your children don't need your help anymore. Maybe they're well settled and they're becoming productive citizens and that's wonderful. But surely there are other children who might need your help. Precisely. I couldn't agree more.

